    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A recurve hunting bow of laminated ash with a hex-rope string, the kind every hex still makes because arrows are free and brass is not. Hunters, scouts and anyone who would rather not announce themselves carry one. It will never out-shoot a Hunting Rifle; it will out-last one, and the ammunition grows on trees.</p><p>Silent two-handed ranged. No signature — it predates the idea.</p>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⚙️ Mechanical Effects</strong></p>\n<p>Two-handed, silent. Arrows can be recovered and re-fletched. No signature ability.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 + 2 Kinetic damage to <em>Integrity</em> <span style=\"opacity:.75\">(arrow)</span></li>\n  <li><strong>Faculty:</strong> Violence</li>\n  <li><strong>Attack:</strong> Firearms (Violence)</li>\n  <li><strong>Range:</strong> 6 / 24 squares</li>\n  <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Scene</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier:</strong> T3</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:END -->\n<!-- BBTTCC:LADDER:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⟡ Circuited (+2). A closed circuit of sigils; it answers one hand.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>+2 to hit and +2 damage</strong> with this weapon (the hit bonus is read from the weapon you swing).</li>\n  <li>Grade raises it to <strong>Tier III</strong> · attuned (one slot).</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:LADDER:END -->"
    }
  },
